  "title": "E6v2 fix round 1: re-gate T-1548's branch with acceptance text that no longer quotes a Python test id as a prose example",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, plan label E6v2-fix1. Fix round of T-1548 (constraints.fix_round_for): this task's branch cuts from task/T-1548, which already carries the complete implementation at commit 06264e4 (acceptance.test_file_paths, acceptance.missing_test_files, the daemon.gate hold with 'FAILED <path> (missing: test file not in task diff)' lines and resume_hint.missing_test_files, plus both tests; the executor reported 253 focused tests green and a clean worktree).\n\nWhy a fix round: the daemon gate held T-1548 gate_red with 'FAILED tests/test_x.py::test_y (missing: test not defined)'. That id came from T-1548's own acceptance TEXT, which quoted it as a prose example of a token the extractor must ignore; acceptance.named_tests parses every tests/<file>.py::name token in the acceptance, so the gate demanded a test that was never meant to exist. This fix round restates the acceptance without that literal. No code defect is known.\n\nWhat to do: on this branch run tests/test_acceptance.py, tests/test_failures.py and tests/test_daemon.py in the foreground. If every test passes, confirm the two acceptance-named tests below exist and post done with the commit sha of the branch head (no new commit is needed). If a test fails, fix it within scope, commit, and re-run. Never background a command and never run the full gate. Do not add a test called test_y and do not create tests/test_x.py.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_acceptance.py::test_missing_test_files_requires_test_paths_in_diff: passes: acceptance.test_file_paths() extracts backend/test/oauth.test.ts, web/src/a.spec.ts, apple/AppTests/FooTests.swift, android/app/src/test/BarTest.kt and a bare tests/test_<name>.py path, but not a Python id carrying a '::' function suffix (owned by missing_tests), not .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh, not globs and not directories; missing_test_files(worktree, acceptance, changed) returns those absent from the worktree or not in changed (changed None means existence only)",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_gate_holds_when_acceptance_test_file_missing_from_diff: passes: daemon.gate holds a done execute task gate_red with resume_hint.missing_test_files and a 'FAILED <path> (missing: test file not in task diff)' failure line, without running tests-green, when its acceptance names backend/test/oauth.test.ts that the task diff does not contain",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
